    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bennetts Auctioneers are delighted to present No. 80 Park Avenue to the market. This magnificent Victorian residence occupies a substantial corner site at the junction of Park Avenue and Sydney Parade Avenue and extends to approximately 373 sq. m. The property retains a wonderful selection of original period features including marble fireplaces, ornate ceiling cornice work, sash windows and attractive bay-windowed elevations. The well-proportioned accommodation of c. 373 sq. m. briefly consists of two elegant interconnecting reception rooms, a study/home office, kitchen/breakfast room, utility room, conservatory, family room, games room/office and five bedrooms, with the principal bedroom incorporating a dressing room and ensuite bathroom. A particularly important feature is the exceptional private gardens and grounds, which extend to approximately 0.44 acres and benefits from a westerly orientation. The property also comes with the significant benefit of full planning permission for a major refurbishment and extension, creating a proposed family home of approximately 564 sq. m. \r\n\r\nNo. 80 Park Avenue stands out for its gardens and grounds, which cover around 0.44 acres. The gardens, which may be accessed by a pedestrian gate off Park Avenue, are set out in lawn with mature shrubbery and trees, providing plenty of solitude and seclusion. The westerly orientation provides plenty of afternoon and evening sunshine. A separate garage and an electronically operated entrance gate from Sydney Parade Avenue provide ample off-street parking to the rear.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\n\r\nSituated on Sandymount’s premier road in this highly sought-after location, No. 80 Park Avenue enjoys an exceptionally convenient location, with Sydney Parade DART Station, Merrion Shopping Centre and St Vincent’s University Hospital all within easy reach. Sandymount Village is just a short stroll away, offering an excellent selection of boutiques, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities, while Sandymount Strand provides a beautiful coastal setting for leisurely walks. The area is particularly well served by a number of highly regarded schools, including St. Michael’s College, Muckross Park, St Andrew’s College, Blackrock College and The Teresian School. Excellent primary schools are also close by, including Star of the Sea, St. Mary’s in Donnybrook and Lakelands. A wide range of sporting and recreational amenities are available nearby, with Herbert Park, Elm Park Golf Club, the RDS and Aviva Stadium all within easy reach. The location offers an excellent balance of convenience, transport links, education, leisure and coastal amenities"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall: 1.90m x 5.10m  Impressive hardwood hall door, tiled floor, feature sliding sash window to the side, decorative ceiling cornice and centre ceiling rose\r\n\r\nDrawing Room: 6.00m x 4.80m  Wood flooring, magnificent bay sash window to the front, feature marble fireplace with stove inset, dado rail, ceiling centre rose and ornate cornicing, double doors leading to the dining room\r\n\r\nDining Room: 4.70m x 4.70m  Wood flooring, centre ceiling rose and double doors leading to the rear garden\r\n\r\nStudy / Home Office: 3.30m x 4.20m  wood flooring, feature bay sash window to the side, attractive marble fireplace, bespoke fitted bookshelves \r\n\r\nGuest W.C.:  Wash hand basin, W.C. and sliding sash window to the side\r\n\r\nLower Hall:  Tiled flooring, understairs storage with feature stained-glass window to the side\r\n\r\nInner Hallway:  1.20m x 7.10m  Tiled flooring, door to rear garden \r\n\r\nGuest W.C.: Tiled flooring, W.H.B., W.C.\r\n\r\nKitchen/ Breakfast room: 4.00m x 6.90m  Tiled flooring, recessed lighting, range of floor and eye-level units, two-ring AGA, ornate tiled splashback, stainless steel double sink, door to utility room\r\n\r\nUtility Room: 3.00m x 2.90m  Fitted press units and door to storage room\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 4.50m x 6.00m   Wood flooring, feature Connemara marble fireplace, double doors to the rear, access to games room\r\n\r\nConservatory: 3.60m x 4.70m  Tiled floor, pleasant outlook over the gardens and double doors to the family room\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFirst floor\r\n\r\nMain Bedroom: 4.70m x 4.80m  Carpet flooring, large sliding sash window overlooking the front gardens towards Park Avenue, generous double bedroom suite with built-in wardrobes\r\n\r\nDressing Room: 1.40m x 3.40m   Carpet flooring, range of fitted units, hanging area and drawers with door to ensuite bathroom\r\n\r\nEnsuite Bathroom: 3.30m x 4.70m  Tiled flooring, dual sink units, feature cast iron roll-top bath, original wash hand basins, bidet and walk-in shower\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 4.00m x 3.30m  Carpet flooring, original sash window to the front\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: 4.20m x 3.40m  Carpet flooring, original sash window to side\r\n\r\nBedroom 4: 3.20m x 4.80m  Carpet flooring, double room with large sliding sash window overlooking the front gardens towards Park Avenue\r\n\r\nBedroom 5: 3.50m x 3.40m  Carpet flooring, Arch to dressing area with two sash windows providing dual aspect and excellent natural light\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom:  tiled flooring, W.H.B., W.C.\r\n\r\nGames Room / Office: 4.60m x 7.00m   Wood flooring and double windows overlooking the rear\r\n\r\n\r\nExterior\r\n\r\nThe gardens and grounds are a particular feature of No. 80 Park Avenue, extending to approximately 0.44 acres. Accessed via a pedestrian gate off Park Avenue, the gardens are laid out in lawn with mature shrubbery and trees, providing a high degree of privacy and seclusion. The westerly orientation provides excellent afternoon and evening sunshine. Ample off-street parking is available to the rear via an electronically operated entrance gate from Sydney Parade Avenue, together with a separate garage.\r\n\r\n\r\nTotal floor area: c. 373 sq. m."
      },
